# README.md — Eman's Code Academy

## 1. Which HTML elements did you use to structure the website?

I used HTML elements such as `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<section>`, and `<footer>` to organize different parts of my website. I also used `<h1>`, `<h2>`, `<h3>`, `<p>`, `<a>`, `<span>`, `<ul>`, and `<li>` to display headings, paragraphs, navigation links, course information, and lists. I used `<div>` elements to group related content, such as course cards, About boxes, and Learning Journey steps.

## 2. How did you arrange the course cards?

I used CSS Grid with `grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr)` to arrange the six course cards into three columns on desktop screens. I used the `gap` property to maintain equal spacing between the cards. For tablet screens, I changed the layout to two columns, and for mobile screens, I arranged the cards in a single column.

## 3. Which CSS property did you find most useful, and why?

I found the `display: grid` property most useful because it helped me arrange the six course cards neatly in rows and columns. It made the layout organized and easier to adjust for different screen sizes. I also used Flexbox to arrange the navigation bar, About section, and Learning Journey steps.

## 4. What problem did you face during development, and how did you solve it?

One problem I faced was arranging the different sections and course cards properly on different screen sizes. Some elements needed adjustments to maintain proper spacing and alignment. I solved this problem by using CSS Grid, Flexbox, and media queries to change the layout for tablet and mobile screens.

## 5. How did you make your website responsive?

I made my website responsive by using CSS Grid, Flexbox, and CSS media queries. I used two breakpoints: 768px for tablet screens and 480px for mobile screens. On tablets, the course cards change to two columns, while on mobile screens, they change to one column. I also adjusted the navigation bar, section padding, and heading sizes to make the website easier to view on smaller devices.

